 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "It may be that purer minds now awake\nThan were before our ancient age:\nThat the tongue's keen glances into\nThe light of God's heart through others\nHave found no less sweet than its own fire,\nAnd kindled more by desire\nThan star or cloud, to make our own\nIts clearness and beauty divine. Moreover,\nThough death seems an enemy divine,\nDeath not in this sense but soon begins mine;\nSoon as I, for whom it began,\nShall go my life with happy",
